{"schema":"cpm-public-practice-bank/1","skills":{"LG 01-ican-1":{"label":"I can choose and justify a strategy for an unfamiliar mathematical puzzle.","questions":[{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-1-R01","prompt":"<p>A mystery number doubles and then increases by 5 to give 23. Explain a strategy for finding it and why it works.</p>","solution":"9; subtract 5, then divide by 2.","answer":"9; subtract 5, then divide by 2."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-1-R02","prompt":"<p>To solve \\(3x+6=24\\), one student subtracts 6 first. Another divides all terms by 3 first. Compare the strategies.</p>","solution":"Both work: x=6; subtracting first yields 3x=18, dividing first yields x+2=8.","answer":"Both work: x=6; subtracting first yields 3x=18, dividing first yields x+2=8."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-1-R03","prompt":"<p>A group says \\(4+2\\times5=30\\). Decide whether its calculation is correct. Explain with the order of operations.</p>","solution":"No: multiply first, so 4+10=14.","answer":"No: multiply first, so 4+10=14."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-1-S01","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Solve.</strong></p><p>\\(5x+7=32\\)</p>","solution":"\\(x=5\\)","answer":"\\(x=5\\)"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-1-S02","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Evaluate.</strong></p><p>\\(7+3(4-2)^2\\)</p>","solution":"19","answer":"19"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-1-S03","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Complete the equation.</strong></p><p>\\(3(\\square+2)=21\\)</p>","solution":"5","answer":"5"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-1-P01","prompt":"<p>Find two different ways to write \\(\\tfrac34\\) as a percent or decimal. Then solve \\(2x+1=9\\).</p>","solution":"0.75, 75%; x=4.","answer":"0.75, 75%; x=4."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-1-P02","prompt":"<p>Solve \\(3(n+2)=24\\).</p>","solution":"\\(n=6\\)","answer":"\\(n=6\\)"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-1-P03","prompt":"<p>Evaluate \\(12-2(3+1)\\). Explain which operation comes first.</p>","solution":"4; evaluate the parentheses, multiply, then subtract.","answer":"4; evaluate the parentheses, multiply, then subtract."}]},"LG 01-ican-2":{"label":"I can represent growth patterns and predict later stages.","questions":[{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-2-R01","prompt":"<p>Study Figures 1–4. Explain how the tile pattern grows. How many tiles will Figure 8 contain?</p><figure class=\"bank-figure\"><img class=\"graph bank-tiles\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" alt=\"Four growing unit-tile figures, starting with four tiles and adding a group of three at each stage\"></figure>","solution":"Add 3 each figure; Figure 8 has 25 tiles.","answer":"Add 3 each figure; Figure 8 has 25 tiles."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-2-R02","prompt":"<p>Rule A is \\(3n+1\\). Rule B is \\(3(n-1)+4\\). Do they describe different patterns? Explain.</p>","solution":"Same rule because 3(n−1)+4=3n+1.","answer":"Same rule because 3(n−1)+4=3n+1."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-2-R03","prompt":"<p>Study Figures 1–4. Write a rule for the number of tiles in Figure \\(n\\). Explain how it fits the pattern.</p><figure class=\"bank-figure\"><img class=\"graph bank-tiles\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" alt=\"Four growing unit-tile figures, starting with six tiles and adding a group of four at each stage\"></figure>","solution":"\\(T(n)=4n+2\\).","answer":"\\(T(n)=4n+2\\)."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-2-S01","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Complete the pattern.</strong></p><table class=\"data-table\"><thead><tr><th>Figure</th><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th><th>4</th><th>5</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Tiles</td><td>2</td><td>6</td><td>10</td><td>14</td><td>?</td></tr></tbody></table><figure class=\"bank-figure\"><img class=\"graph bank-tiles\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"data:image/svg+xml;base64,\" alt=\"Four unit-tile arrangements with each successive figure containing four more tiles\"></figure>","solution":"18","answer":"18"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-2-S02","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Write a rule.</strong></p><p>3, 8, 13, 18, … ; figure \\(n\\)</p>","solution":"\\(5n-2\\)","answer":"\\(5n-2\\)"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-2-S03","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Find the number of tiles in Figure 10.</strong></p><p>5, 8, 11, 14, …</p>","solution":"32","answer":"32"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-2-P01","prompt":"<p>A pattern starts 7, 11, 15, … . Find Figure 6. Then solve \\(3x-2=16\\).</p>","solution":"27; x=6.","answer":"27; x=6."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-2-P02","prompt":"<p>Continue the pattern \\(5,9,13,17,\\ldots\\) for two more terms.</p>","solution":"\\(21,25\\)","answer":"\\(21,25\\)"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-2-P03","prompt":"<p>Figure counts are \\(6,10,14,18\\). Find the number of tiles in Figure 7.</p>","solution":"30 tiles.","answer":"30 tiles."}]},"LG 01-ican-3":{"label":"I can investigate how the graph of a quadratic function changes.","questions":[{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-3-R02","prompt":"<p>For \\(y=(x-2)^2-1\\), compare the outputs at \\(x=1\\) and \\(x=3\\). Why are they equal?</p>","solution":"Both are 0; x=1 and x=3 are equally distant from x=2.","answer":"Both are 0; x=1 and x=3 are equally distant from x=2."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-3-R03","prompt":"<table class=\"data-table\"><thead><tr><th>x</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A</td><td>1</td><td>3</td><td>5</td><td>7</td></tr><tr><td>B</td><td>1</td><td>2</td><td>5</td><td>10</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Which relationship changes by a constant amount? Which has constant second differences?</p>","solution":"A linear, first differences 2; B quadratic, second differences 2.","answer":"A linear, first differences 2; B quadratic, second differences 2."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-3-S01","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Evaluate.</strong></p><p>\\(y=x^2-4\\), \\(x=3\\)</p>","solution":"5","answer":"5"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-3-S02","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Complete the table.</strong></p><table class=\"data-table\"><thead><tr><th>x</th><th>-2</th><th>-1</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>2</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>y=x²</td><td>?</td><td>?</td><td>?</td><td>?</td><td>?</td></tr></tbody></table>","solution":"4,1,0,1,4","answer":"4,1,0,1,4"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-3-S03","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Identify the minimum.</strong></p><table class=\"data-table\"><thead><tr><th>x</th><th>-2</th><th>-1</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>2</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>y</td><td>5</td><td>2</td><td>1</td><td>2</td><td>5</td></tr></tbody></table>","solution":"Minimum y=1 at x=0.","answer":"Minimum y=1 at x=0."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-3-P01","prompt":"<p>Evaluate \\(x^2-2\\) at \\(x=-2,0,2\\). Then continue 4, 9, 14, … two terms.</p>","solution":"2, −2, 2; 19, 24.","answer":"2, −2, 2; 19, 24."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-3-P02","prompt":"<p>For \\(y=x^2-1\\), find \\(y\\) when \\(x=-2\\).</p>","solution":"\\(3\\)","answer":"\\(3\\)"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-1-3-P03","prompt":"<p>A parabola has vertex \\((0,-3)\\). Where is the vertex after shifting the graph up 5 units?</p>","solution":"\\((0,2)\\)","answer":"\\((0,2)\\)"}]},"LG 01-ican-4":{"label":"I can describe what a graph communicates about a situation.","questions":[{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-1-S02","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Find the vertical change.</strong></p><p>From (2,7) to (6,15). Vertical change?</p>","solution":"8","answer":"8"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-1-P01","prompt":"<p>At times 0, 1, 2, 3, distances are 2, 5, 8, 11. Predict time 4. Then evaluate \\(2x+1\\) at \\(x=3\\).</p>","solution":"14; 7.","answer":"14; 7."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-1-P02","prompt":"<p>A distance table shows 2, 6, 10, 14 meters at times 0, 1, 2, 3 seconds. Find the distance at 4 seconds.</p>","solution":"18 meters.","answer":"18 meters."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-1-P03","prompt":"<p>At times 0, 2, 4 minutes, the water depths are 10, 10, 10 centimeters. What does the unchanged depth mean?</p>","solution":"The water level stayed the same.","answer":"The water level stayed the same."}]},"LG 01-ican-5":{"label":"I can interpret cube-root and absolute-value relationships.","questions":[{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-2-R02","prompt":"<p>A student claims \\(|-6|=-6\\). Explain why the claim is incorrect.</p>","solution":"Absolute value is distance from zero, so |-6|=6.","answer":"Absolute value is distance from zero, so |-6|=6."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-2-R03","prompt":"<p>What input gives output 4 for \\(y=\\sqrt[3]{x}\\)? Explain using a cube.</p>","solution":"x=64 because 4³=64.","answer":"x=64 because 4³=64."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-2-S01","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Evaluate.</strong></p><p>\\(|-9|+|-2|\\)</p>","solution":"11","answer":"11"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-2-S02","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Evaluate.</strong></p><p>\\(\\sqrt[3]{-125}\\)</p>","solution":"−5","answer":"−5"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-2-S03","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Solve.</strong></p><p>\\(|x|=7\\)</p>","solution":"x=7 or x=−7","answer":"x=7 or x=−7"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-2-P01","prompt":"<p>Evaluate \\(|-5|\\) and \\(\\sqrt[3]{27}\\). Then write the next two terms: 2, 6, 10, …</p>","solution":"5, 3; 14, 18.","answer":"5, 3; 14, 18."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-2-P02","prompt":"<p>Evaluate \\(|-7|+|3|\\).</p>","solution":"\\(10\\)","answer":"\\(10\\)"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-2-P03","prompt":"<p>Find the number whose cube is \\(-64\\).</p>","solution":"\\(-4\\)","answer":"\\(-4\\)"}]},"LG 02-ican-1":{"label":"I can use input-output rules to represent relationships.","questions":[{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-3-R01","prompt":"<table class=\"data-table\"><thead><tr><th>Input</th><th>-1</th><th>0</th><th>2</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Output</td><td>1</td><td>3</td><td>7</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Describe an operation rule that works for every pair.</p>","solution":"Multiply the input by 2, then add 3.","answer":"Multiply the input by 2, then add 3."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-3-R02","prompt":"<p>Rules A and B are \\(2x+1\\) and \\(x+3\\). At which input do they give the same output?</p>","solution":"At x=2, both equal 5.","answer":"At x=2, both equal 5."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-3-R03","prompt":"<p>A machine adds 4 to an input, then squares the result. Explain why \\((x+4)^2\\) matches but \\(x^2+4\\) does not.</p>","solution":"Order matters: square the whole sum, not only x.","answer":"Order matters: square the whole sum, not only x."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-3-S01","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Complete the table.</strong></p><table class=\"data-table\"><thead><tr><th>x</th><th>-2</th><th>0</th><th>4</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>\\(y=3x-1\\)</td><td>?</td><td>?</td><td>?</td></tr></tbody></table>","solution":"−7, −1, 11","answer":"−7, −1, 11"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-3-S02","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Evaluate.</strong></p><p>\\(f(x)=2x+5\\); \\(f(-3)\\)</p>","solution":"−1","answer":"−1"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-3-S03","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Write a rule.</strong></p><p>Inputs 0,1,2 give outputs 4,7,10.</p>","solution":"\\(y=3x+4\\)","answer":"\\(y=3x+4\\)"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-3-P01","prompt":"<p>If \\(y=2x-1\\), list outputs for \\(x=0,1,2\\). Then solve \\(2n+3=11\\).</p>","solution":"−1, 1, 3; n=4.","answer":"−1, 1, 3; n=4."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-3-P02","prompt":"<p>A function machine triples the input and subtracts 2. What output comes from input 5?</p>","solution":"\\(13\\)","answer":"\\(13\\)"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-3-P03","prompt":"<p>A machine adds 4 and then doubles the result. The output is 18. Find the input.</p>","solution":"\\(5\\)","answer":"\\(5\\)"}]},"LG 02-ican-2":{"label":"I can distinguish functions from relationships that are not functions.","questions":[{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-4-R01","prompt":"<p>The pairs are \\((1,4),(2,6),(1,7)\\). Is this relation a function? Explain.</p>","solution":"No; input 1 has two outputs.","answer":"No; input 1 has two outputs."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-4-R02","prompt":"<p>Pairs \\((1,5),(2,5),(3,5)\\) all have output 5. Is this a function? Explain.</p>","solution":"Yes; repeated outputs are allowed, but each input has exactly one output.","answer":"Yes; repeated outputs are allowed, but each input has exactly one output."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-4-S01","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Function or not?</strong></p><p>\\((0,1),(2,3),(0,4)\\)</p>","solution":"Not a function.","answer":"Not a function."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-4-S02","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Identify the repeated input.</strong></p><table class=\"data-table\"><thead><tr><th>x</th><th>-1</th><th>2</th><th>-1</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>y</td><td>3</td><td>5</td><td>8</td></tr></tbody></table>","solution":"x=−1","answer":"x=−1"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-4-P01","prompt":"<p>Is \\((1,3),(2,3),(3,3)\\) a function? Evaluate \\(2(-3)+5\\).</p>","solution":"Yes; −1.","answer":"Yes; −1."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-4-P02","prompt":"<p>Does \\(\\{(1,2),(1,3),(2,4)\\}\\) represent a function? Explain.</p>","solution":"No; input 1 has two different outputs.","answer":"No; input 1 has two different outputs."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-4-P03","prompt":"<p>For \\(y=2x-5\\), find the output when \\(x=-1\\).</p>","solution":"\\(-7\\)","answer":"\\(-7\\)"}]},"LG 02-ican-3":{"label":"I can identify the domain and range of a relation.","questions":[{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-5-R01","prompt":"<p>Tickets cost $6 each, and at most 8 tickets may be bought. What inputs are reasonable for the total-cost rule?</p>","solution":"Whole numbers 0 through 8.","answer":"Whole numbers 0 through 8."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-5-R02","prompt":"<table class=\"data-table\"><thead><tr><th>x</th><th>-2</th><th>0</th><th>2</th><th>4</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>y</td><td>5</td><td>1</td><td>5</td><td>9</td></tr></tbody></table><p>List the domain and range without repetitions.</p>","solution":"Domain {−2,0,2,4}; range {1,5,9}.","answer":"Domain {−2,0,2,4}; range {1,5,9}."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-5-R03","prompt":"<p>The function \\(f(x)=\\sqrt{x}\\) has real outputs. Explain why negative inputs are excluded.</p>","solution":"The real square root of a negative number does not exist.","answer":"The real square root of a negative number does not exist."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-5-S01","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>List the domain.</strong></p><p>\\((2,5),(4,7),(6,5)\\)</p>","solution":" {2,4,6}","answer":" {2,4,6}"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-5-S02","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>List the range.</strong></p><p>\\((2,5),(4,7),(6,5)\\)</p>","solution":" {5,7}","answer":" {5,7}"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-5-S03","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>List the possible inputs.</strong></p><p>A parking garage has levels 1 through 5. List the possible level inputs.</p>","solution":"{1,2,3,4,5}","answer":"{1,2,3,4,5}"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-5-P01","prompt":"<p>For \\(f(x)=x+2\\) with inputs \\(\\{-1,0,3\\}\\), list its outputs. Then extend 4, 9, 14, … one term.</p>","solution":"{1,2,5}; 19.","answer":"{1,2,5}; 19."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-5-P02","prompt":"<p>Find the domain of \\(\\{(-3,1),(0,4),(2,7)\\}\\).</p>","solution":"\\(\\{-3,0,2\\}\\)","answer":"\\(\\{-3,0,2\\}\\)"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-1-2-5-P03","prompt":"<p>Find the range of \\(\\{(1,4),(2,4),(3,-1)\\}\\).</p>","solution":"\\(\\{-1,4\\}\\)","answer":"\\(\\{-1,4\\}\\)"}]},"LG 02-ican-4":{"label":"I can connect linear growth in tables, graphs, and equations.","questions":[{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-1-R03","prompt":"<table class=\"data-table\"><thead><tr><th>x</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>A</td><td>1</td><td>4</td><td>7</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>B</td><td>1</td><td>4</td><td>9</td><td>16</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Which is linear? Give numerical evidence.</p>","solution":"A; it adds 3 each time. B changes by 3,5,7.","answer":"A; it adds 3 each time. B changes by 3,5,7."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-1-S01","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Find the slope.</strong></p><p>Points (1,3) and (5,11)</p>","solution":"2","answer":"2"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-1-S02","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Complete the table.</strong></p><table class=\"data-table\"><thead><tr><th>x</th><th>0</th><th>1</th><th>2</th><th>3</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>y</td><td>4</td><td>7</td><td>10</td><td>?</td></tr></tbody></table>","solution":"13","answer":"13"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-1-S03","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Write an equation.</strong></p><p>Slope 4; y-intercept −2.</p>","solution":"\\(y=4x-2\\)","answer":"\\(y=4x-2\\)"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-1-P01","prompt":"<p>Find the change per step for outputs 5, 9, 13, 17. Is \\((1,2),(2,2),(1,3)\\) a function?</p>","solution":"4; not a function.","answer":"4; not a function."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-1-P02","prompt":"<p>A table has \\(x=0,1,2,3\\) and \\(y=3,7,11,15\\). Write a rule.</p>","solution":"\\(y=4x+3\\)","answer":"\\(y=4x+3\\)"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-1-P03","prompt":"<p>The outputs 2, 5, 8, 11 increase by a constant amount. What is the change per step?</p>","solution":"\\(3\\)","answer":"\\(3\\)"}]},"LG 02-ican-5":{"label":"I can calculate and interpret slope as a constant rate of change.","questions":[{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-2-R01","prompt":"<p>A tank has 12 L at minute 1 and 27 L at minute 6. Find and interpret its average rate of change.</p>","solution":"(27−12)/(6−1)=3 L/min; tank gains 3 liters per minute.","answer":"(27−12)/(6−1)=3 L/min; tank gains 3 liters per minute."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-2-R02","prompt":"<p>One line has slope −2 and another has slope 3. Compare their directions and rates.</p>","solution":"First decreases 2 per 1; second increases 3 per 1.","answer":"First decreases 2 per 1; second increases 3 per 1."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-2-S01","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Find the slope.</strong></p><p>(−2,1), (2,9)</p>","solution":"2","answer":"2"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-2-S02","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Find the rise.</strong></p><p>(3,−4) to (7,5)</p>","solution":"9","answer":"9"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-2-S03","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Find the run.</strong></p><p>(−1,8) to (6,10)</p>","solution":"7","answer":"7"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-2-P01","prompt":"<p>Find the slope through (0,3) and (4,11). Then evaluate \\(f(2)\\) for \\(f(x)=3x-1\\).</p>","solution":"2; 5.","answer":"2; 5."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-2-P02","prompt":"<p>Find the slope through \\((0,2)\\) and \\((3,8)\\).</p>","solution":"\\(2\\)","answer":"\\(2\\)"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-2-P03","prompt":"<p>As \\(x\\) rises by 4, \\(y\\) falls by 12. Find the slope.</p>","solution":"\\(-3\\)","answer":"\\(-3\\)"}]},"LG 03-ican-1":{"label":"I can compare vertical and horizontal changes to find slope.","questions":[{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-3-S01","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Calculate the slope.</strong></p><p>(0,−5) to (4,3)</p>","solution":"2","answer":"2"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-3-S02","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Find the slope.</strong></p><p>Rise −6, run 3</p>","solution":"−6/3=−2","answer":"−6/3=−2"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-3-P01","prompt":"<p>Find rise/run from (−2,1) to (2,−3). Then find \\(y\\) when \\(x=4\\) in \\(y=2x+1\\).</p>","solution":"rise −4, run 4, slope −1; y=9.","answer":"rise −4, run 4, slope −1; y=9."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-3-P02","prompt":"<p>Find \\(\\Delta y\\) and \\(\\Delta x\\) from \\((1,3)\\) to \\((4,9)\\).</p>","solution":"\\(\\Delta y=6,\\;\\Delta x=3\\)","answer":"\\(\\Delta y=6,\\;\\Delta x=3\\)"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-3-P03","prompt":"<p>Find the slope between \\((-2,5)\\) and \\((2,-3)\\).</p>","solution":"\\(-2\\)","answer":"\\(-2\\)"}]},"LG 03-ican-2":{"label":"I can write and interpret linear equations in slope-intercept form.","questions":[{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-4-R03","prompt":"<p>Does \\(y=3x+2\\) pass through (2,8) and (4,15)? Explain.</p>","solution":"(2,8) yes; (4,15) no because y=14.","answer":"(2,8) yes; (4,15) no because y=14."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-4-S01","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Write an equation.</strong></p><p>Slope \\(−3\\), intercept \\(4\\).</p>","solution":"\\(y=−3x+4\\)","answer":"\\(y=−3x+4\\)"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-4-S02","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Find the y-intercept.</strong></p><p>\\(y=5x−7\\)</p>","solution":"−7","answer":"−7"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-4-S03","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Find the slope.</strong></p><p>\\(y=−\\tfrac12 x+6\\)</p>","solution":"−1/2","answer":"−1/2"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-4-P01","prompt":"<p>Write an equation with slope 2 and intercept −5. Decide if \\((0,1),(1,4),(0,2)\\) is a function.</p>","solution":"y=2x−5; not a function.","answer":"y=2x−5; not a function."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-4-P02","prompt":"<p>Write an equation of a line with slope \\(-2\\) and y-intercept \\(5\\).</p>","solution":"\\(y=-2x+5\\)","answer":"\\(y=-2x+5\\)"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-1-4-P03","prompt":"<p>For \\(y=3x-4\\), find the y-intercept.</p>","solution":"\\((0,-4)\\)","answer":"\\((0,-4)\\)"}]},"LG 03-ican-3":{"label":"I can interpret slope in a motion situation.","questions":[{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-1-S01","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Calculate the average speed.</strong></p><p>24 miles in 3 hours</p>","solution":"8 mi/h","answer":"8 mi/h"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-1-S02","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Find the distance.</strong></p><p>Speed 5 m/s for 7 s</p>","solution":"35 m","answer":"35 m"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-1-S03","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Find the slope.</strong></p><p>(0,12),(4,28)</p>","solution":"4","answer":"4"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-1-P01","prompt":"<p>Distance from a marker follows \\(d=3t+2\\). Find \\(d(4)\\), slope, and y-intercept.</p>","solution":"14; slope 3; intercept 2.","answer":"14; slope 3; intercept 2."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-1-P02","prompt":"<p>A car travels \\(d=4t+3\\) meters after \\(t\\) seconds. Find \\(d\\) at \\(t=5\\).</p>","solution":"23 meters.","answer":"23 meters."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-1-P03","prompt":"<p>Distance increases from 2 meters to 14 meters in 3 seconds. Find the average rate.</p>","solution":"4 meters per second.","answer":"4 meters per second."}]},"LG 03-ican-4":{"label":"I can compare and explain rates of change in context.","questions":[{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-2-R01","prompt":"<p>Plan A grows by $8 every 2 weeks. Plan B grows by $15 every 3 weeks. Compare their weekly rates.</p>","solution":"A=$4/week; B=$5/week; B is faster.","answer":"A=$4/week; B=$5/week; B is faster."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-2-R02","prompt":"<p>Temperature changes from 18°C to 6°C over 4 hours. Find the rate and interpret its sign.</p>","solution":"−3°C/hour; cooling by 3°C each hour.","answer":"−3°C/hour; cooling by 3°C each hour."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-2-R03","prompt":"<p>A student says a car traveling 120 miles in 2 hours averages 240 mph. Explain the error.</p>","solution":"120÷2=60 mph, not 240.","answer":"120÷2=60 mph, not 240."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-2-S01","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Compare the unit rates.</strong></p><p>18 km in 3 h; 28 km in 4 h</p>","solution":"6 km/h vs 7 km/h; second greater.","answer":"6 km/h vs 7 km/h; second greater."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-2-S02","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Find the unit price.</strong></p><p>$42 for 6 notebooks</p>","solution":"$7/notebook","answer":"$7/notebook"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-2-S03","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Find the speed.</strong></p><p>120 meters in 30 seconds</p>","solution":"4 m/s","answer":"4 m/s"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-2-P01","prompt":"<p>A line rises 9 when x increases 3. Find slope. Another rate is 2.5 per x-unit. Which is greater?</p>","solution":"3; first is greater.","answer":"3; first is greater."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-2-P02","prompt":"<p>Runner A travels 18 meters in 3 seconds. Runner B travels 20 meters in 4 seconds. Who has the greater rate?</p>","solution":"Runner A; 6 m/s versus 5 m/s.","answer":"Runner A; 6 m/s versus 5 m/s."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-2-P03","prompt":"<p>A tank fills at 7 liters per minute. How much is added in 5 minutes?</p>","solution":"35 liters.","answer":"35 liters."}]},"LG 03-ican-5":{"label":"I can write a linear equation from a real-world situation.","questions":[{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-3-R01","prompt":"<p>A taxi charges $4 to start plus $2 per mile. Write an equation for fare and interpret its terms.</p>","solution":"C=2m+4; $2/mile and $4 starting fee.","answer":"C=2m+4; $2/mile and $4 starting fee."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-3-R02","prompt":"<table class=\"data-table\"><thead><tr><th>Hours</th><th>0</th><th>2</th><th>4</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cost ($)</td><td>15</td><td>25</td><td>35</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Write an equation and interpret the intercept.</p>","solution":"C=5h+15; $15 initial charge.","answer":"C=5h+15; $15 initial charge."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-3-R03","prompt":"<p>A delivery fee follows \\(C=3m+6\\). A customer predicts $21 for 5 miles. Is the prediction correct?</p>","solution":"Yes; 3(5)+6=21.","answer":"Yes; 3(5)+6=21."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-3-S01","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Write an equation.</strong></p><p>Initial 9, grows 4 per step.</p>","solution":"y=4x+9","answer":"y=4x+9"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-3-S02","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Find the starting value.</strong></p><p>\\(C=7n+12\\)</p>","solution":"12","answer":"12"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-3-S03","prompt":"<p class=\"skill-direction\"><strong>Evaluate.</strong></p><p>\\(C=5x+3\\); \\(x=6\\)</p>","solution":"33","answer":"33"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-3-P01","prompt":"<p>Write a rule for outputs 7, 11, 15 at inputs 0,1,2. Then give the y-intercept and slope.</p>","solution":"y=4x+7; intercept 7; slope 4.","answer":"y=4x+7; intercept 7; slope 4."},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-3-P02","prompt":"<p>A taxi costs $6 plus $2 per mile. Write a rule for the cost \\(C\\) after \\(m\\) miles.</p>","solution":"\\(C=2m+6\\)","answer":"\\(C=2m+6\\)"},{"id":"ALG1-AP1-2-2-3-P03","prompt":"<p>A line is given by \\(y=-3x+8\\). Find \\(y\\) at \\(x=2\\).</p>","solution":"\\(2\\)","answer":"\\(2\\)"}]}}}
